// declaration-without-value.wlg: every variable has a value from its declaration on.
// There is no undefined: a declaration says what its variable starts as, null if nothing else.

var total;
total = 5;

/* Errors:
declaration-without-value.wlg(4,5): error WL1006: 'total' needs a value where it is declared: 'var total = …;'.
*/
